174	   rule working where :user-invalid isn't supported: in a plain selector list, one
175	   unsupported selector drops the whole rule. */
176	:is(:user-invalid, .user-invalid-fallback) {
177	  border-color: #d93025;
178	  background-color: #fce8e6;
179	}
180	
181	:is(:user-invalid, .user-invalid-fallback) + .error-msg {
182	  display: block;
183	}
184	```
