716	--- Guide for required-field-feedback ---
717	# Required Field Feedback
718	
719	## The Problem
720	Marking required fields with an error state immediately upon page load can be confusing. Ideally, a required field should only look "invalid" if the user has attempted to fill it out and failed.
721	
722	## The Solution
723	The `:user-invalid` pseudo-class solves this perfectly. For a required field, it will not match on page load. It will only match if:
724	1.  The user interacts with the field (e.g., types a character and deletes it) and then leaves it (blur), leaving it empty.
725	2.  The user attempts to submit the form while the field is empty.
726	
727	### Implementation Strategy
728	
729	1.  **HTML Constraint**: Add the `required` attribute to your inputs.
730	2.  **Visual Feedback**: Use `:user-invalid` to style the border red and show a "Required" helper text.
731	3.  **Timing**: Rely on the browser's native timing for visual feedback. You don't need `onBlur` handlers to add a `touched` class anymore, though some JavaScript is still needed to sync ARIA attributes (see below).
732	4.  **Error Text**: Show visible error text with the error styling, so the error isn't shown by color alone. Start each message with an error icon that has a text alternative such as "Error" (the safest choice), or word every message as an error, for example "Name is required.", and use the same approach for every error in the form.
733	5.  **Error Link**: List the error message in the field's `aria-describedby` only while the field is invalid, so screen readers read it with the field. A reference in the markup would read the hidden message from page load. The script in section 3 does this for each field whose `data-error` attribute is set to its error message's `id`.
734	
735	## Implementation Guide
736	
737	### 1. HTML Structure
738	```html
739	<form id="feedback-form">
740	  <div class="field">
741	    <label for="full-name">Full Name</label>
742	    <!-- Set data-error to the error message's id. The aria-invalid script lists that id in aria-describedby while the field is invalid. -->
743	    <input
744	      type="text"
745	      id="full-name"
746	      name="full-name"
747	      required
748	      data-error="name-error"
749	    >
750	    <!-- MANDATORY: Include an icon or distinct non-color indicator alongside error text -->
751	    <div id="name-error" class="error-msg">
752	      <span role="img" aria-label="Error">❌</span> This field is required.
753	    </div>
754	  </div>
755	</form>
756	```
